LTO on SunOS: CMakeLists.txt turns on CMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION
whenever check_ipo_supported() passes, which it does with gcc 14 on illumos
and Solaris. But the link-editor there has no LTO plugin, and every shared
object -- renderer_opengl1/2.so and the game modules -- is linked empty
(8 KB, only libc NEEDED, no GetRefAPI/vmMain); executables happen to work.
Leave LTO off on SunOS, and respect -DCMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION=
given on the command line (it was overridden by a normal variable).

Upstream: not submitted yet; no issue or pull request about it at
https://github.com/ioquake/ioq3 (checked 2026-11-10).

--- ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/CMakeLists.txt.orig
+++ ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,10 +42,14 @@
   set(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE Release)
 endif()
 
-# Try to enable LTO by default
+# Try to enable LTO by default, unless it was set on the command line.
+# Not on SunOS: gcc's LTO needs the linker plugin, which the illumos and
+# Solaris link-editor lacks; check_ipo_supported() still passes there, but
+# every shared object (renderers, game modules) comes out empty.
 include(CheckIPOSupported)
 check_ipo_supported(RESULT IPO_SUPPORTED)
-if(IPO_SUPPORTED)
+if(IPO_SUPPORTED AND NOT DEFINED CMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION
+   AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "SunOS")
     set(CMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE)
     set(CMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION_DEBUG FALSE)
 endif()
